                   are TRANSFER volumes into aqueous urea (J. Chem. Thermodyn. 32 (2000)
                   1409) and into aqueous NaCl (34 (2002) 1825) - neither is a
                   water-only V0 and neither can be this source.";
    whyItFits     "the record's temperature, 298.15 K, was carried in phase 3 WITHOUT a
                   source stating it; 298.15/308.15/318.15 K is exactly this paper's
                   temperature set, which independently explains where the 298.15 K came
                   from and makes the identification self-consistent";
    access        "Royal Society of Chemistry, closed; Unpaywall is_oa = false
                   (checked 2026-07-24).  No repository copy.";
    action        "obtain the article (inter-library loan) and CONFIRM the V0 digit and
                   the temperature against its table before the citation above is written
                   into provenance{} or the record is promoted.  If the digit does not
                   match, the number in this file has no known source at all and must be
                   deleted with a structured absence, exactly as phase D deleted the 48
